  "slug": "ai-agents-biological-4390",
  "summary": "Predictors for protein yield, drug resistance and binder behavior are now checked against measured or diagnostic outcomes rather than accepted as single outputs.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is testing structure-informed predictions against experimental or diagnostic readouts rather than accepting a single predicted output. A massively parallel pooled assay quantifies E. coli monomeric yield for more than 39,000 proteins, providing a benchmark for inverse folding and training the ESMC-MonoYield predictor. Leave-one-out cross-validated classifiers predict artemisinin resistance in P. falciparum Kelch13 mutants from structure-derived physicochemical features. The de novo SARS-CoV-2 RBD binder study uses AlphaFold, MD, docking and SAP signatures to diagnose failure modes behind trade-offs between target binding and self-association. The new element is the emphasis on multi-criteria validation, where designed or predicted properties are assessed against measured yield, resistance or self-association behavior.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-10"
}
